# Reusable helper — authenticate through the Nafath happy path and land on an
# authenticated Home.
#
# CONTRACT
#   NATIONAL_ID - the National ID / Iqama to sign in with.
# Precondition: the app is running and unauthenticated (a cleared launch, or after a
# logout). Postcondition: Home greets the account holder by name.
#
# SCOPE
# This is the happy path only. The AUTH-002 input-validation cases and the AUTH-009
# restart check stay owned by login.yaml and are deliberately not duplicated here - this
# helper exists so journey flows stop re-inlining the sign-in sequence, not to take those
# cases over. login.yaml is unchanged.
appId: fi.iwa.sakani
name: Login with National ID
---
# SAFETY GUARD - never type an unresolved or malformed ID. Without this, a caller that forgot
# to pass NATIONAL_ID would type the literal text "undefined" into the login field.
# Dollar-free on purpose - see the fail-fast guard in full-journey.yaml: a "$" inside ${...}
# makes Maestro 2.9.0 skip evaluation and pass the assert unconditionally.
- assertTrue: ${typeof NATIONAL_ID !== "undefined" && String(NATIONAL_ID).length === 10 && !/[^0-9]/.test(String(NATIONAL_ID)) && (String(NATIONAL_ID).charAt(0) === "1" || String(NATIONAL_ID).charAt(0) === "2")}
# Get to the guest Home. A cleared launch replays onboarding and this build interposes a
# "Marketplace Day" sheet whose scrim hides the sign-in entry entirely.
- runFlow:
    file: clear-overlays.yaml
    env:
      ANCHOR: "(?s).*Login / Sign up.*"

- extendedWaitUntil:
    visible: "(?s).*Login / Sign up.*"
    timeout: 120000
- tapOn: "(?s).*Login / Sign up.*"

# Build PRE-4.7.5-1279 spells this "Nefath" on the button and STG-4.7.5-1278 spells it
# "Nafath" (defect D-14), so both are matched.
- extendedWaitUntil:
    visible: "Continue with N[ae]fath"
    timeout: 45000

# The field hint carries a comma before "or" in this build.
- tapOn: "Enter your ID, phone number,? or email"
- inputText: ${NATIONAL_ID}
- assertVisible: ${NATIONAL_ID}
- tapOn: "Continue"

# SAFETY VALIDATION - the Nafath screen must carry EXACTLY the requested ID before the session
# is created. Maestro text selectors are full-match regexes, so a different ID - including a
# stale default that silently won over an override - cannot satisfy this line. This is the
# last point at which a wrong account can be stopped before it is authenticated.
- extendedWaitUntil:
    visible: "Login with nafath"
    timeout: 45000
- assertVisible: ${NATIONAL_ID}
# Record the ID this helper has just proven on the Nafath screen. The Full Journey compares it
# with the ID it resolved at the start before any destructive stage runs (the identity gate at
# the end of its STAGE 1). A caller that never reaches this line has no record, and that gate
# fails.
- evalScript: ${output.loginNationalId = String(NATIONAL_ID)}
- tapOn: "Confirm"

- extendedWaitUntil:
    notVisible: "Login with nafath"
    timeout: 90000

# The promo sheet, the biometrics prompt and the contact-details prompt all land after
# authentication, in any order and not on every run.
#
# This is the ONE caller that opts out of the helper's exit contract (its final wait for
# ANCHOR): the weekly-deal promo handled just below can legitimately still cover Home when
# the helper returns, and this caller recovers from it itself with a relaunch. The opt-out
# is an explicit `output` flag, set immediately before this single call and cleared
# immediately after it, so it cannot apply to any other caller.
#
# THE ANCHOR ALSO STOPS ON THE PROMO (10/09/2026). The helper loops `while notVisible:
# ANCHOR`, and nothing inside that loop can clear the promo on this build: its Back handler
# does not close it, and while the keyboard covers it no handler matches at all. With the
# greeting as the only anchor, the loop spent all 20 passes (~5 minutes) doing nothing
# before the recovery below got its turn. Full-journey run 2026-09-10_150206 (1119880062)
# sat on exactly that stack from its Nafath "Confirm" until it was stopped at 15:07:16 -
# the moment the loop ran out. With the promo's title and its control as alternatives, the
# helper hands back as soon as the promo is up and the keyboard guard and relaunch below
# engage at once. The greeting is still the real destination: it is asserted by name at
# the end of this file, and nothing after this call trusts the anchor alone.
- evalScript: ${output.anchorOptional = true}
- runFlow:
    file: clear-overlays.yaml
    env:
      ANCHOR: '(?si)((Hello|Good (morning|afternoon|evening)),\s*\S.*|New service|Go to the weekly (offer|deal))'
- evalScript: ${output.anchorOptional = false}
# The "Sakani sharrai / Weekly deal" promo exposes NO dismiss control: its only clickable node
# is the "Go to the weekly deal" CTA (re-checked live on 14/09/2026, PRE-4.7.6-1283 - the whole
# sheet is "New service", "Sakani sharrai", its two lines of copy and that CTA, and unlike the
# NPS sheet it has neither a close "X" nor a clickable scrim). It has been seen both as a
# FULL-SCREEN interstitial (bounds [0,132]-[1080,2337]) and as a "New service" bottom sheet over
# the contact screen - same content, same single control.
#
# ANDROID BACK DOES CLOSE IT on this build, so it is dismissed rather than relaunched around
# (14/09/2026). Captured live with the sheet on screen and no automation running: one Back left
# the app in the foreground with the sheet gone and the contact screen - which the helper below
# clears - underneath (evidence/2026-09-14-weekly-promo: promo-sheet.xml, after-01-back.xml).
# The earlier note here said Back did not work; that was the keyboard-covered state handled just
# above, where the first Back only closes the keyboard. The CTA is NEVER tapped - that would
# navigate into the offer instead of dismissing it.
#
# Bounded at three Backs, each one guarded by the promo still being visible, and the promo must
# be gone afterwards: no relaunch, and no app restart is caused by this popup at all. The only
# launchApp left in this file is the login-page recovery further down, which is a different case.
# KEYBOARD-COVERED PROMO - the post-login deadlock, reproduced live on 10/09/2026 (1000011487).
# The "Number and Email Already Linked" screen mounts with its phone field focused, the promo
# sheet is shown on top of it, and the soft keyboard - raised by that focused field, and drawn
# above every app window - covers the sheet, hiding the promo's only control, "Go to the weekly
# deal". In screen frames taken every 3s, all three appeared together 8-12s after Confirm. The
# contact screen's own handler cannot match either, because the modal sheet removes that screen
# from the hierarchy. Nothing could fire, and the greeting wait below simply ran out.
#
# One Android Back closes the keyboard and exposes the control (verified: before - sheet plus
# keyboard; after one Back - the sheet with "Go to the weekly deal" visible), so the relaunch
# recovery below can engage as designed. Guarded to exactly that state - the promo's title is
# visible and its control is not - so it cannot fire anywhere else. Escape does NOT close this
# keyboard (tried: no change). "Update information" is never touched.
- runFlow:
    when:
      visible: "New service"
    commands:
      - runFlow:
          when:
            notVisible: "Go to the weekly (offer|deal)"
          commands:
            - back
            - waitForAnimationToEnd:
                timeout: 3000
- runFlow:
    when:
      visible: "Go to the weekly (offer|deal)"
    commands:
      - evalScript: "${console.log('LOGIN - weekly-deal promo is up; closing it with Back, no relaunch')}"
      - repeat:
          times: 3
          while:
            visible: "Go to the weekly (offer|deal)"
          commands:
            - back
            - waitForAnimationToEnd:
                timeout: 4000
      - assertNotVisible: "Go to the weekly (offer|deal)"
      - runFlow:
          file: clear-overlays.yaml
          env:
            ANCHOR: '(?si)(Hello|Good (morning|afternoon|evening)),\s*\S.*'

# CONTACT PROMPT OVER THE LOGIN PAGE - back on the login page while signed in (13/09/2026).
# After Nafath "Confirm" the contact-details prompt ("Update your contact information" /
# "Number and Email Already Linked") is not always stacked on Home. When the weekly promo has
# already appeared, Home is underneath and the helper's dismissal of the prompt reveals it
# (7 of 7 runs). When the promo has NOT appeared yet, the prompt can sit directly on the login
# page this subflow typed into, and the same guarded dismissal reveals THAT page - its own back
# arrow, "Continue with Nafath", the National ID still in the field - although the session is
# already authenticated (3 of 3 runs: 2026-09-10_095858 and 2026-09-10_113110 for 1000011487,
# 2026-09-13_094738 for 1119880044). No handler matches that page, so the helper spent its 20
# passes and the greeting wait its 90 s on a static screen - about 5 minutes that looked like a
# hang - and the run then failed on the greeting.
#
# Relaunch recovers it - verified live from that exact screen on 13/09/2026: launchApp without
# clearState, the CSAT survey (its "Dismiss" is handled by clear-overlays; Submit is never
# tapped), then "Hello, <name>". Safe for the same reason as the promo recovery above: it runs
# only here, straight after this subflow's own authentication, and relaunch keeps the session
# that was just established, so it cannot switch accounts - the caller still proves the
# account by National ID afterwards. It runs at most once, and the login form is never
# re-submitted: if the session did not survive, the greeting wait below fails on the login page.
- runFlow:
    when:
      visible: "Continue with N[ae]fath"
    commands:
      - evalScript: "${console.log('LOGIN RECOVERY - back on the login page after authentication, relaunching with state kept')}"
      - launchApp
      - runFlow:
          file: clear-overlays.yaml
          env:
            ANCHOR: '(?si)(Hello|Good (morning|afternoon|evening)),\s*\S.*'


# Authenticated. Home must greet the user BY NAME: STG-4.7.5-1278 renders "Hello, <name>"
# where PRE-4.7.5-1279 rendered "Good Morning, <name>", so both are matched. The ",\s*\S"
# tail is load-bearing and is deliberately not relaxed to a bare "Hello" - the greeting has
# to be followed by an actual name, which is what separates an authenticated header from a
# guest one, since the guest Account renders "Hello" with nothing after it.
- extendedWaitUntil:
    visible: '(?si)(Hello|Good (morning|afternoon|evening)),\s*\S.*'
    timeout: 90000
- assertNotVisible: "(?s).*Login / Sign up.*"
